# Reverse proxy in front of the dashboard container. Caddy's whole reason
# for being here is that it gets and renews a Let's Encrypt certificate for
# CADDY_DOMAIN automatically -- no certbot, no manual renewal cron.
#
# CADDY_DOMAIN is a free sslip.io hostname (163-172-155-168.sslip.io) that
# just resolves to the Instance's own IP -- that's enough for Let's Encrypt,
# which only needs a real domain name it can look up, not anything owned or
# registered. If a real domain gets pointed at this box later, changing
# CADDY_DOMAIN in the deploy .env is the only thing that needs to change.
#
# Plain HTTP still works (Caddy answers ACME's http-01 challenge on :80 and
# also redirects any other :80 traffic to https automatically) -- so this
# also incidentally fixes the original problem: browsers hitting :80 get
# redirected straight to the encrypted version instead of a rewritable
# plaintext response.

{$CADDY_DOMAIN} {
	reverse_proxy dashboard:3000
}
